// apps/rtq's fourth query: FCPW's closest silhouette point
// (Scene::findClosestSilhouettePoint; bvh.slang's findClosestSilhouettePoint)
// over the set of silhouette edges of its normal cone hierarchy -- the query
// the walk on stars asks for its star radius (apps/wosx/wost.bonsai). A file
// of its own, imported by the programs that have the set (snch.bonsai here,
// wost.bonsai in apps/wosx): rtq.bonsai's programs over a plain tree of
// triangles have no silhouette edges, and with the extern set declared here
// they need no layout for it. Declared over elements.bonsai and
// metrics/fcpw_scalar.bonsai, whose silhouette section has the arithmetic
// (the cone test, the edge test, the record).
//
// Written as `trace` is written (queries.bonsai): the test an edge has to
// pass is the query's `intersects` -- within the radius and a silhouette
// from the center -- which the tree bounds with its own form over the cone
// box (FCPW's child test: cone valid, box within the radius, cone
// overlapping the view cone), and the key the nearest passes by is
// `distmin`, the edge's squared distance; the argmin is over a filter and
// answers none where no edge passes, the common case (an argmin over every
// element of a set has an element, and the query would otherwise have to
// call every edge a candidate). The map annotates each candidate with
// FCPW's record of it, the closest point on the edge and its distance, the
// same computation the test and the key make, so the leaf makes it once.
// What FCPW does that this does not: stop once a silhouette within the
// query's minimum radius is found, since its caller clamps the answer to
// that radius and any such silhouette gives the same answer; the exact
// closest is found here and the clamp is the caller's (apps/wosx/PLAN.md,
// "The silhouette query read against FCPW's", has the two traversals side
// by side).
extern silhouettes : set[Edge];

func closest_silhouette(q : SilhouetteQuery) -> option[(Edge, SilhouetteHit)] {
    return argmin(|e : Edge, h : SilhouetteHit| distmin(q, e),
                  filter(|e : Edge, h : SilhouetteHit| intersects(q, e),
                         map(|e : Edge| (e, silhouette_record(q, e)), silhouettes)));
}
